{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789314362,"nonce":"NzHMPdSKYjzywEF5htiYWWFbZPU=","title":"Python: a list annotated with a class type holds addresses, not boxes","message":"`bodies: list` lowered to `List(Object)`: every element boxed, every `b.x` a dynamic `py$getattr$x`, every `b.vx * b.mass` a `zb_any_arith`. The nbody port ran 10x slower than CPython.\n\n`list[Body]` now lowers to `Ty::List(Elem::Class(k))`: a list of instance addresses (`Kind::Ptr` in the shared library, `usize` elements, suffix `ptr`). Element reads cast the address back to `Ty::Class(k)`, so field access and arithmetic are the typed struct paths. `Elem::Class` flows through `elem_ir` / `elem_call` / `elem_arg` / `expr_as_elem` in `lower.rs`, at every list operation that reads or writes an element (index, pop, get, set, membership, comprehension push, append, insert, remove, index, count, min, max).\n\nBoxing an element when it must become `Any` (printing the list, iterating it dynamically, storing it in a dict) goes through `zb_hook_box_instance(p)`, a hook the frontend defines: it reads the class index from the instance's `$class` field and boxes under the class's tag. The library declares the hook extern when `policy.instance_hooks` is set and as a raw function-pointer box otherwise. `Kind::Ptr` arms were added to `zb_any_iter`, `zb_seq_repr_any` and `zb_seq_len_any`; `\u003c` on two addresses is a fatal TypeError, as on two instances without `__lt__`.\n\nTyped nbody after this and the inliner change (b69e72e): 10M steps in about 0.85 s against CPython's 45 s and ZynML nbody_ref's 0.57 s.\n\nLeft open: an unannotated `bodies: list` or a bare `bodies = [Body(...), ...]` still infers `List(Object)`. Inferring the element type from a homogeneous literal, and a parameter's type from its call sites, is the next lever (nbody_plain runs 2.2 s, all of it dynamic dispatch).","files":null}]}